    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey quick question i'm doing my end of year bookkeeping for my freelance design work and i'm stuck on something. i just bought a really expensive ergonomic office chair for my studio setup. does that count as a business expense/deduction or is it considered a personal draw? trying to figure out how to categorize it in quickbooks. thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A high-quality ergonomic chair for your studio setup is generally considered a business expense, not a personal draw, as it's necessary for your work. You should categorize it as \"Office Equipment\" or \"Furniture and Fixtures\" in QuickBooks. If the chair is very expensive, you might need to consider depreciating it over several years, which is a more complex accounting procedure. It's best to check with a tax professional to ensure you categorize it correctly for your specific situation.",
      "source": "target",
