    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay that makes sense. i think i'll go with furniture and fixtures. but what about smaller stuff? like i keep losing track of these tiny little miscellaneous receipts for things like printer ink or even just random office supplies i buy at target. it feels like money just disappears sometimes and it's making my reconciliation a mess. is there a better way to track those small stuff expenses so they dont just get lost?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For those tiny, miscellaneous receipts, the best practice is to use a dedicated system to capture them immediately, before they vanish into the ether. You can use a mobile app—many accounting software platforms have one—to snap a picture of the receipt right after you buy the ink or supplies. Then, you can batch-enter those expenses into QuickBooks later, grouping them under a category like \"Office Supplies.\" This prevents the small items from becoming a massive, chaotic pile of paper cluttering your desk.",
      "source": "target",
